# Third-party code keeps its upstream formatting: the vendored libraries in
# lib/ (lib/.clang-format also disables formatting there) and the musl libc
# headers. clang-format skips these files even when they are passed on the
# command line (as CI does). "**" is not recursive in clang-format 19, so
# every directory depth is listed.
lib/*
lib/*/*
lib/*/*/*
lib/*/*/*/*
include/libc/*
include/libc/*/*
include/libc/*/*/*
